---
id: boiled-roasted-buckwheat
title: Boiled Roasted Buckwheat
category: modular_carb

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 178

storage:
  fridge_days: 5
  freezer_friendly: true

equipment:
  - saucepan
---

Optionally rinse @roasted-buckwheat{67%g} quickly under cold running tap water in a fine-mesh strainer and drain thoroughly.

In a #saucepan, combine the drained buckwheat, 160 ml (2/3 cup) cold water, and @kosher-salt{0.25%tsp}. Bring to a vigorous boil over medium-high heat.

Once boiling, reduce the heat to low, cover tightly with a lid, and simmer undisturbed for ~simmer-time{11%min} until all surface water has been absorbed. Do not stir during cooking to keep the groats fluffy and intact.

Remove the pot from the heat. Keep covered with the lid on and let steam undisturbed for ~steam-time{5%min} to complete cooking and stabilize texture.

Uncover the saucepan, add @unsalted-butter{1%tsp}, and fluff gently with a fork until the butter is completely melted and evenly distributed. Transfer the entire cooked portion (178 g cooked yield) to a meal prep container and let cool before sealing.
